 to the initial value problem is\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{-t}.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302281 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ad687230-8844-51e9-a75a-cfbd2d9890e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186302281 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=5 \\\\ {c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n5{c}_{1}=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n2\\cdot 1+{c}_{2}=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324223 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}6{e}^{28}+18{e}^{-7} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324223 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324223 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1def90c1-295c-513f-8d17-08d3eb728d5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325296 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}18{e}^{28}+24{e}^{-7} \\\\ -6{e}^{28}+18{e}^{-7}\\end{alig