stem of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2}=6 \\\\ -{c}_{1}+3{c}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second equation by $-1$ and adding the result to the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{c}_{2}=6.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-{c}_{1}+4\\cdot 6=6\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=18.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =18\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+6\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate $x(7)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(7) & =[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4\\cdot 7}+[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-7} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}]{e}^{28}+[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-7} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-18{e}^{28}+24{e}^{-7} \\\\ -18{e}^{28}+18{e}^{-7}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370043 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370043 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370043 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370043 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370043 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370043 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370043 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370043 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186370044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370043 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f9a329d6-e958-5db1-9f6a-f6e439f8337a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370044 #edb/ref 1080 "x(t)=5[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370044 #edb/