igenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=0.$*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370065 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1f87900f-7ab3-5049-8d96-2a75cd0b00fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370065 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write down the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for the given system:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-1\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=0.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3/2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}=5 \\\\ {c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{c}_{2}=14\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${c}_{2}=-14$ into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}-2(-14)=9\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=37.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =37[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}-14[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370066 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370066 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370066 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370066 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370066 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370066 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370066 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370066 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186370067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370066 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3ea9e031-e55c-53ff-bb1f-586d3945e9f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370067 #edb/ref 1080 "x(t)=37[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}-14[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370067 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370067 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2b9bda6e-7e9f-5f46-a9ff-034b8fce5b51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186370068 #edb/ref 